# Implementation Plan - HOTFIX-014 — Remove Unwanted Application Settings

Simplify the Application Settings UI screen by removing non-essential user-facing settings sections while preserving full backward compatibility for saved settings and keeping the Overlay Visibility controls fully functional.

## Proposed Changes

### UI Presentation Layer

#### [MODIFY] [settings_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/settings_panel.py)
- Remove user-facing settings widgets and group boxes:
  - Appearance Theme group box (`_combo_theme`, `_spin_font_scale`)
  - General Options group box (`_chk_updates`, `_chk_restore`)
  - Typing Engine Settings group box (`_spin_speed`, `_spin_pre_delay`, `_chk_jitter`)
- Embed `OverlayVisibilityPanel` directly into `SettingsPanel` layout under the "Application Settings" header.
- Connect `OverlayVisibilityPanel` transparency changes to `ConfigManager` (`appearance.overlay_transparency`).
- Ensure vertical spacing, margins, and scroll area layout are clean, compact, and visually balanced.

---

### Data Models & Backward Compatibility Layer

#### [MODIFY] [settings.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/models/settings.py)
- Preserve default field definitions in `AppearanceSettings`, `GeneralSettings`, and `TypingSettings` to ensure 100% backward compatibility when loading legacy `settings.json` files containing obsolete fields (`theme`, `font_scale`, `check_updates`, `restore_session`, `default_speed`, `pre_typing_delay`, `jitter_enabled`).

---

### Unit Tests

#### [MODIFY] [test_settings_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/tests/unit/test_settings_panel.py)
- Update test cases to verify:
  - Appearance Theme, General Options, and Typing Engine controls are no longer rendered in `SettingsPanel`.
  - `OverlayVisibilityPanel` is present inside `SettingsPanel`.
  - Updating transparency in `SettingsPanel` updates `ConfigManager` and emits transparency signals.
  - Legacy `settings.json` containing obsolete fields loads without validation errors.

